{"assets":["/statement-assets/12808c09ce4d66c0798e8932ebbd451a8d63355630d1d1376a28f6c7d9865945.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"906","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Party"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Arseny likes to organize parties and invite people to it. However, not only friends come to his parties, but friends of his friends, friends of friends of his friends and so on. That's why some of Arseny's guests can be unknown to him. He decided to fix this issue using the following procedure."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At each step he selects one of his guests "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":", who pairwise introduces all of his friends to each other. After this action any two friends of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":" become friends. This process is run until all pairs of guests are friends."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Arseny doesn't want to spend much time doing it, so he wants to finish this process using the minimum number of steps. Help Arseny to do it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 22"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/12808c09ce4d66c0798e8932ebbd451a8d63355630d1d1376a28f6c7d9865945.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of guests at the party (including Arseny) and the number of pairs of people which are friends."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ u, v ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u ≠ v"},{"kind":"text","text":"), which means that people with numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" are friends initially. It's guaranteed that each pair of friends is described not more than once and the graph of friendship is connected."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print the minimum number of steps required to make all pairs of guests friends."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second line print the ids of guests, who are selected at each step."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple solutions, you can output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 6\n1 2\n1 3\n2 3\n2 5\n3 4\n4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n2 3 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 4\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n1 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case there is no guest who is friend of all other guests, so at least two steps are required to perform the task. After second guest pairwise introduces all his friends, only pairs of guests "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(4, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(4, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" are not friends. Guest "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" can introduce them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case guest number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a friend of all guests, so he can pairwise introduce all guests in one step."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"906C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/906/problem/C"}